.TH FILESYNC 1 "April 2026" "" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
filesync \- map and sync files across git checkouts
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B filesync
.RI [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.br
.B filesync
.RI [ help | \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B filesync
.I subcommand
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B filesync
is a Bash CLI that keeps global repo and collection metadata under a system directory (default
.BR ~/.filesync\-root )
and per-project file mappings under
.BR .filesync/files.json .
It discovers the project from the current working directory: first by matching registered repo checkouts that contain
.BR .filesync/files.json ,
then by walking parent directories, similar to
.BR git .
With no arguments,
.B filesync
prints a short usage summary and exits.

The dispatcher resolves its install root via
.B BASH_SOURCE
and
.B readlink
or
.B realpath
so a symlinked
.B PREFIX/bin/filesync
still finds package
.B lib/
and
.BR share/ .

If the first argument begins with a hyphen and is not a known subcommand (for example
.BR \-\-dry\-run ),
it is passed to
.B sync
as if you had run
.BR "filesync sync" .
The same dispatch accepts the
.B s
alias.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the program version and exit.
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage and exit.
.PP
With a subcommand first, the same
.B \-h
and
.B \-\-help
flags print extended usage for that subcommand only (see each command below).
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.SS "Project setup"
.TP
.B init
[\fIdirectory\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-repo\fR]
Create
.B .filesync/files.json
as an empty array at the project root and ensure the system metadata store exists (default
.BR ~/.filesync\-root ;
override with
.BR FILESYNC_HOME ).
Default directory is the current working directory.
.B init
does not walk parents; the given directory establishes the project root.
If
.B .filesync/files.json
already exists,
.B init
exits with an error.
When stdin is a terminal and
.B \-\-no\-repo
is not given, prompts to append a repo definition to global
.B repos.json
(name, remote URL, branch, stable id).
The checkout
.B path
is stored relative to your home directory when possible (git work tree top when inside git, otherwise the project root), with defaults for name, URL, and branch taken from git when the project is inside a work tree.
If stdin is not a terminal, that step is skipped (use
.B "new repo"
.RB ( n " " \-r )
later, or pass
.B \-\-no\-repo
to suppress the notice).
.TP
.B config
Inspect or change system metadata:
.B show
prints effective system home, repo path anchor, and global JSON paths;
.B doctor
summarizes environment overrides, reports duplicate
.B name
entries in global
.BR repos.json ,
and checks that each
.B path
field resolves to an existing directory (relative paths use the repo path anchor).
When the current working directory is inside a filesync project, it also validates
.BR files.json
(duplicate
.BR local_path ,
unknown
.BR repo_id ),
compares coupled
.B kind=clone
marker tokens
.RI ( path= ", " repo= ", " repo_id=)
to each row and the global catalog, reports clone markers with no mapping row, and scans for
.B kind=master
files whose canonical master has no tracked clone rows (see
.BR "filesync info file" ).
Output is grouped into sections with a short summary of warnings and notes;
.B set progress
.RI ( hidden | bar | percent ;
TTY progress style in
.BR preferences.json )
updates
.BR preferences.json
(see
.BR "filesync config --help" ).
Per-repo
.B check_sync_enabled
and
.B mirror_in_enabled
are changed with
.BR "filesync edit repo" .
The standalone
.B progress
command is removed; use
.B "config set progress"
or inspect
.B "config show"
for the effective value.
.B set repo-path-root
is no longer supported; relative
.B path
values resolve under
.B $HOME
(or
.B FILESYNC_REPO_PATH_ANCHOR
for tests).
.TP
.B migrate
If the discovered project still has per-project
.B repos.json
,
.B collections.json
, or
.BR config.json ,
merge them into the global store and remove those files after backup under
.BR .filesync/legacy-backup/ .
Repos already present in the global catalog are matched by
.B name
only; the existing global row is kept when path, URL, or branch differ (a notice is printed).
Also ensures every global repo has an
.B id
and every known
.I files.json
row has
.BR repo_id ,
and every global repo row has boolean
.B merge_using_git
(git work tree probe at the checkout path when the field was missing).
.TP
.B handle-missing
Non-interactive repair for rows whose master or local paths are missing (see
.B "filesync handle-missing --help" ).
.SS "Inspect and sync"
.TP
.B check
Also
.BR c .
.RI [ \-\-repo= name ]
.RI [ \-\-file= fragment " ..." ]
.RI [ \-\-repo\-file= fragment " ..." ]
.RI [ \-\-all\-files= fragment " ..." ]
.RI [ \-\-status= list ]
Verify mappings, refresh
.I files.json
row status (including per-row
.IR last_check_at ).
Optional
.BI \-\-repo=
filters to one repo by name.
.BI \-\-file=
may be repeated; when at least one fragment is nonempty after trimming, a row must have its project-relative
.I local_path
contain one of the fragments (substring).
.BI \-\-repo\-file=
may be repeated; when nonempty, the row's
.I repo_file_path
must contain one of the fragments.
.BI \-\-all\-files=
may be repeated; when nonempty, the row must match at least one fragment against
.I local_path
or
.IR repo_file_path .
These three dimensions combine with logical AND when more than one is active; omit a flag entirely (or pass only blank values) to leave that dimension unconstrained.
.BI \-\-status=
matches rows by cached
.I sync_status
before recomputing selected rows.
Token rules match
.BR sync :
literal statuses,
.IR unset ,
.IR all ,
and
.I error
for any
.IR error_* .
Compares each local file to the clone rendered from the master copy (diff drives
.IR sync_status ).
Per-row status lines use the same layout as
.BI list " files" :
.IR [ sync_status "] " repo " | " repo_file_path
with an optional local path arrow and
.B ⚠
comma-separated
.I check_marker_warnings
codes when needed (crossover, local missing
.IR kind=clone ", "
master missing
.IR kind=master ", "
etc.).
Codes are also stored in
.IR files.json ;
those situations are not fatal on their own.
If the master file cannot be rendered, the row is
.I error_master_marker
but the command exits successfully unless other blocking issues exist.
When standard error is a terminal,
.I progress_display
in merged preferences is not
.B hidden
(see
.BR "config show"
and
.BR "config set progress" ),
and at least 10 rows are in the configuration,
.B check
may draw a scanning progress indicator on standard error; per-row lines go to standard output, so output may not stay fixed on one line.
.TP
.B info
Also
.BR i .
.PP
With
.B \-\-help
or
.B \-h
as the only argument
.RI ( e.g. \*(lqfilesync info \-\-help\*(rq " or \*(lqi \-h\*(rq),
prints combined usage for
.I info file
and
.I info repo
forms.
.PP
.RI [ file " | " \-f ]
.I path
.RI [ \-\-fix\-marker ]
The optional
.B file
or
.B \-f
word selects the same subcommand explicitly; you may omit it after
.B i
.RI ( e.g. \*(lqfilesync i \fIpath\fR\*(rq).
Resolve
.I path
to a tracked clone in the current project's
.I files.json
or to the canonical master file under a registered repo checkout
.RI ( master-at-checkout ).
Lists every
.I files.json
row in the union of this project and other registered checkouts that share the same master
.RI ( repo_file_path
and repo identity),
runs
.B check
with
.B \-\-file=
for those rows in each affected project,
then prints a summary on standard error with
.BR "Role: master"
or
.BR "Role: clone" ,
the canonical master key, and related
.I files.json
rows.
If the canonical master file's
.B kind=master
marker does not match whether any clones are tracked, prompts on a terminal to add or strip the marker; with standard input not a terminal, prints a hint unless
.B \-\-fix\-marker
is given to perform the update without prompting.
Exits with the same status as
.B check
when
.B check
reported blocking issues (after printing).
.RS
.PP
.BR "info repo" ", " "info \-r"
.I repo-name
.RI ( "and " "i repo" / "i \-r" )
prints global catalog fields for
.IR repo-name ,
verifies the checkout directory exists (same path resolution as
.BR "config doctor" ),
reports how many
.I files.json
rows in the current project reference that repo, and summarizes their
.B sync_status
values (run
.B check
with
.BI \-\-repo=
to refresh).
Exits unsuccessfully if
.I repo-name
is not in global
.BR repos.json .
.RE
.TP
.BR "retarget " clone " | " retarget " " \-c
.I local-clone new-repo-file-path
.RI [ \-\-move " | " \-\-mv ]
Update
.I repo_file_path
after
.B git mv
on the master in the checkout.
.I local-clone
must be a
.B tracked clone
in the current project (resolution matches
.BR "info file" ;
only that row is updated).
.I new-repo-file-path
is repo-relative, must exist, and must carry
.BR kind=master .
Without
.BR \-\-move " / " \-\-mv ,
the row is marked
.IR sync_required
and the local file remains at
.IR local_path .
With
.BR \-\-move " / " \-\-mv ,
the local file is moved to
.I new-repo-file-path
(project-relative) and
.I local_path
is updated.
For every sibling mapping across projects, use
.BR "retarget " master
instead.
.TP
.BR "retarget " master " | " retarget " " \-m
.I local-master "|" old-repo-path " " new-repo-file-path
.RI [ \-\-move " | " \-\-mv ]
Update
.I repo_file_path
for
.B every
mapping that shares this canonical master (same multi-project union as
.BR "info file " / " remove repo" ).
.I local-master
is the master file under a registered checkout when it still exists on disk (resolution matches
.BR "info file" ).
If the first path no longer exists after
.BR git mv ,
filesync may anchor from
.I new-repo-file-path
when it uniquely identifies a
.B kind=master
file in a registered checkout (otherwise pass an existing master path).
.I new-repo-file-path
must exist in the checkout with
.BR kind=master .
If
.I files.json
still lists stale paths,
.B retarget master
may infer the old
.I repo_file_path
from missing master files in the checkout.
Without
.BR \-\-move " / " \-\-mv ,
each row is marked
.I master_file_moved
so consumers can run
.BR "sync \-\-move" .
With
.BR \-\-move " / " \-\-mv ,
each affected local file is moved and
.I local_path
is updated;
.B \-\-move
is rejected when more than one mapping for that master exists in the same project
.RI ( destination " collision).
.PP
.BR "filesync " retarget
with no further selector prints compound help for
.B clone
and
.BR master .
.TP
.B sync
Also
.BR s .
.RI [ \-\-repo= name ]
.RI [ \-\-file= fragment " ..." ]
.RI [ \-\-repo\-file= fragment " ..." ]
.RI [ \-\-all\-files= fragment " ..." ]
.RI [ \-c " | " \-\-check ]
.RI [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RI [ \-f " | " \-\-force ]
.RI [ \-\-showall ]
.RI [ \-\-status= list ]
.RI [ \-\-include\-detached ]
.RI [ \-\-move " | " \-\-mv ]
Copy from master repos into the project and update
.IR files.json .
Filters
.BI \-\-repo= ","
.BI \-\-file= ","
.BI \-\-repo\-file= ","
and
.BI \-\-all\-files=
(same rules as
.BR check )
apply before syncing.
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check
runs
.B check
first with the same path-filter and
.BI \-\-status=
arguments; if that preflight fails, sync exits without copying.
By default only rows with unset,
.IR sync_required ", " error_missing_local ", or " master_file_moved
status are considered; detached rows are skipped unless
.BR \-\-include\-detached .
.BR \-\-move ", " \-\-mv
runs first for selected rows whose status is
.IR master_file_moved :
when
.I local_path
differs from
.IR repo_file_path ,
the local file is moved into place, the row's
.I local_path
is updated, and status becomes
.I sync_required
before the usual copy-from-master step.
With
.BR \-\-dry\-run ,
a planned move is reported and that row is not processed further in the same run.
.BI \-\-status=
overrides with a comma-separated list of
.I sync_status
tokens (any token may match): literals
.RI ( synced ", " sync_required ", " detached ", ...),
.I unset
for empty status,
.I all
for every status except
.IR detached ,
unless
.B \-\-include\-detached
is set or
.I detached
appears in the list,
.I error
for any status whose name starts with
.IR error_ .
.B \-\-dry-run
prints planned work without writing files or status.
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
overwrites a local file that lacks a clone marker.
When no
.B \-\-status
filter is given,
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
also selects
.I local_newer
and
.I conflict
rows so master replaces the local copy.
.B \-\-showall
prints a per-file line for rows that are already in sync with master; by default those lines are omitted (counts in the summary still include them).
Coupled sync requires a master marker on the repo file.
When a repo's
.B merge_using_git
is true and the project directory is a git work tree, there must be no changes except possibly this project's
.I files.json
(usually
.BR .filesync/files.json ) ;
any other dirty path blocks this path.
.B sync
records content updates and refreshed
.I files.json
on a short-lived branch, commits them together, and merges into the previous branch (up to three merge attempts may exclude paths that conflict), so the work tree is clean after a successful batch.
Per-file lines start with a result symbol, use the same
.IR repo " | " repo_file_path
layout as
.BI list " files" ,
and end with a bracketed outcome
.RI ( e.g. "\fB[Synced]\fR", "\fB[Already in sync]\fR", "\fB[Dry-run]\fR" ).
Rows skipped by status filter or marker rules are printed in gray.
Like
.BR check ,
a TTY progress indicator on standard error may appear when scanning many rows; per-file sync lines go to standard output, so output may not stay fixed on one line.
If no repos are configured (for example global
.I repos.json
is an empty array),
.B sync
exits with failure.
.TP
.BI list " repos"
Also
.BR "l " \-r .
.RI [ \-\-repo= name ]
List configured repos or details for one repo by name.
Accepts only
.BR \-\-repo= ;
it does not accept path filters
.RI ( \-\-file= ", " \-\-repo\-file= ", " \-\-all\-files= ),
.BR \-\-status= ", or " \-\-include\-detached .
.TP
.BI list " files"
Also
.BR l ", " "l " \-f .
.RI [ \-\-repo= name ]
.RI [ \-\-file= fragment " ..." ]
.RI [ \-\-repo\-file= fragment " ..." ]
.RI [ \-\-all\-files= fragment " ..." ]
.RI [ \-\-status= list ]
.RI [ \-\-include\-detached ]
List file mappings and cached status; run
.B check
to refresh status fields. Filters match
.BR check .
If filters match no rows, prints nothing and exits successfully.
With no
.B list
sub-target,
.B l
alone lists files the same as
.BR "list files" .
Optional
.BI \-\-status=
uses the same comma-separated tokens as
.BR sync
(including
.B \-\-include\-detached
with
.IR all ).
Non-empty
.I check_marker_warnings
for a row are summarized on the line after the status.
.TP
.BI list " collections"
Also
.BR "l " \-col .
List named repo collections from the global
.I collections.json
.RI ( FILESYNC_HOME ).
These names can be used in
.B \-\-also=
with
.BR "add " file ", " "add " master ", and " "add " clone ,
and as the primary
.I target_repo
for
.BR "add " clone
(subject to expansion rules in that section).
For
.BR "add " file
and
.BR "add " master ","
only single-member collections are accepted in the primary repo slot (same resolution rules as
.BR \-\-also= ).
Accepts no options.
.SS "Mappings and repos"
.TP
.BI add " file"
Also
.BR a ", " "a " \-f .
.I repo_name path_in_repo \fR[\fI:local_path\fR] \fR...
.RI [ \-\-mark\-master ]
.RI [ \-\-also= names ]
The first argument
.I repo_name
must resolve to exactly one global repo: a name in
.B repos.json
or a collection in
.B collections.json
that lists exactly one repo (multi-member collections are rejected; specify the source repo explicitly and use
.BR \-\-also= ).
Track files from a repo checkout into the project. Each path token is relative to the repo; append
.IB : local_path
when the project-relative path differs.
The repo file must carry a
.B kind=master
marker; if it has a different filesync marker (for example
.BR kind=clone ),
the command fails.
If the repo file has no filesync marker at all, the command fails unless
.B \-\-mark\-master
is given, in which case a master marker line is prepended (comment style follows the path extension).
The local file is written (or overwritten) with content rendered from the master copy including a
.B kind=clone
marker.
.B \-\-also=
mirrors the mapping into other initialized projects. Each comma-separated token is either a repo name from global
.B repos.json
whose resolved checkout directory is a sibling project root containing
.BR .filesync/files.json ,
or a collection name defined in global
.B collections.json
(expanded to that collection's repo names in order). Collection and repo names share a single namespace (no name may be both). Empty collections cannot be used with
.BR \-\-also= .
Targets whose resolved checkout equals the current project root are skipped; each target must have
.B mirror_in_enabled
true (default).
For each sibling project, filesync resolves checkouts using the configured path anchor (home directory, or
.B FILESYNC_REPO_PATH_ANCHOR
in tests) and writes/overwrites the clone file under that sibling project's root.
.TP
.BI add " master"
Also
.BR "a " \-m .
.I target_repo local_path \fR[\fI:path_in_repo\fR] \fR...
.RI [ \-\-also= names ]
The first argument
.I target_repo
must resolve to exactly one global repo (repo name or a single-member collection); multi-member collections are rejected (use an explicit master repo and
.BR \-\-also= ).
Promote local files into the master repo and add mappings. Omit
.IB : path_in_repo
when the master path matches
.IR local_path .
With
.BR \-\-also= ,
filesync mirrors mapping rows into sibling projects but initializes those mirrored rows as
.B sync_required
so each project can run
.B check
or
.B sync
to validate timestamps and status in its own context.
.TP
.BI add " clone"
Also
.BR "a " \-c .
.I target_repo master_path \fR[\fI:local_path\fR] \fR...
.RI [ \-\-also= names ]
The first argument
.I target_repo
is a repo name or a collection name (expanded like
.BR \-\-also= );
multiple targets from the primary argument and
.B \-\-also=
are merged (deduplicated), then the same skip and
.B mirror_in_enabled
rules apply as for
.BR "add " file .
Add a
.B kind=clone
copy and
.I files.json
row in a sibling initialized project, using a
.B kind=master
file that lives under the current project root.
Each
.I master_path
token is project-relative; append
.IB : local_path
to write the clone at a different path in the target project (the clone marker
.B path=
still uses
.IR master_path ).
If the source file has no filesync marker, a
.B kind=master
marker is prepended automatically (comment style follows the path extension); other non-master markers are rejected.
The target project's
.B repo=
token and row
.B repo_name
are inferred from global
.B repos.json
by finding the repo entry whose configured checkout path resolves to this project root.
The command fails if the target local file already exists or if
.I files.json
already lists that
.IR local_path .
.B \-\-also=
mirrors the same operation into additional sibling projects (same rules as
.BI add " file" ).
.TP
.B push
.RI [\-\-all]
.I local_path \fR[\fIlocal_path ...\fR]
.RI [ \-\-to\-clones path " [" \-\-dry\-run ]]
Push local clone content to the master path in the linked repo (reverse of default
.BR sync ).
With
.BR \-\-all ,
also pushes every mapping whose
.I sync_status
in
.I files.json
is
.BR local_newer ;
if no
.I local_path
arguments are given, only those rows are selected.
If both
.B \-\-all
and explicit
.I local_path
arguments are given, the union is pushed (each path once).
If
.B \-\-all
is given, no paths are listed, and there are no
.B local_newer
rows, the command exits successfully after a short notice.
.PP
.B \-\-to\-clones
.I path
propagates the canonical master (resolved like
.BR "info file" )
into every tracked clone row that shares the same master across the union of project roots: for each affected project it runs
.B sync
with
.BR \-c ", " \-\-check
(so row status is refreshed before selection),
.BR \-\-repo= ","
one
.B \-\-file=
per affected clone
.BI local_path
in that project,
.BR \-f ","
and
.BI \-\-status= all
.RI ( plus
.B \-\-dry\-run
when given).
Do not combine
.B \-\-to\-clones
with
.B \-\-all
or other
.I local_path
arguments;
.B \-\-dry\-run
is only valid with
.BR \-\-to\-clones .
If no related clone rows exist, exits successfully after a short notice.
.TP
.BI detach " file"
Also
.BR d ", " "d " \-f .
.I local_path \fR[\fIlocal_path ...\fR]
Set
.I sync_status
to
.I detached
in
.IR files.json
and rewrite the first marker line in each local file to
.BR kind=detached
(keeping path/repo context when possible).
.TP
.BI attach " file"
Also
.BR da ", " "da " \-f .
.I local_path \fR[\fIlocal_path ...\fR]
Re-couple detached rows and run
.B check
on each.
.TP
.BI detach " files-in-repo"
Also
.BR "d " \-fir .
.I repo_name
For every row in
.I files.json
whose
.I repo_name
matches
.IR repo_name ,
run the same operation as
.BI detach " file"
for that row's
.IR local_path .
.TP
.BI attach " files-in-repo"
Also
.BR "da " \-fir .
.I repo_name
For every such row, run the same operation as
.BI attach " file"
(non-detached rows are skipped as for
.BI attach " file" ).
.TP
.BI remove " file"
Also
.BR rm ", " "rm " \-f .
.RI [ \-\-all-missing ]
.I local_path \fR[\fIlocal_path ...\fR]
Remove the matching row(s) from
.IR files.json .
On disk, removes
.B kind=clone
or
.B kind=detached
marker line(s) from each local file; leaves
.B kind=master
lines so a shared master copy can stay valid for other projects.
.B \-\-all-missing
adds every mapping whose cached
.I sync_status
is
.BR error_missing_master
(union with any explicit
.IR local_path
arguments); if it is the only selector and there are no such rows, the command exits successfully after a short message.
.TP
.BI remove " repo"
Also
.BR "rm " \-r .
.I repo_name
.RI [ \-y " | " \-\-yes ]
.RI [ \-\-force ]
Remove the named repo from
.IR repos.json
after removing every
.I files.json
mapping for that repo across all known projects (registered checkouts with
.BR .filesync/files.json ,
plus the current project).
The repo name is also removed from every entry in
.I collections.json
and any collection that becomes empty is dropped.
If there are no mappings anywhere, the repo entry is removed immediately.
If any mapping exists anywhere, you must pass
.B \-\-force
first; then the command prompts for confirmation unless
.B \-y
or
.B \-\-yes
is given.
Discovery matches
.B sync :
the union of registered checkouts that contain
.BR .filesync/files.json
and the current project root.
Local file contents are not deleted except via marker stripping as in
.BI remove " file" .
.TP
.BI new " repo"
Also
.BR "n " \-r .
Interactively add a repo definition to
.IR repos.json .
The checkout
.B path
is derived from the current directory (git work tree top when inside git, otherwise the working directory), relative to home when possible.
Run from that checkout.
The name must not duplicate an existing repo entry and must not match a collection name in
.IR collections.json .
.TP
.BI edit " repo"
Also
.BR "e " \-r .
.I repo_name
.RI [ \-\-rename= name ]
.RI [ \-\-path= path ]
.RI [ \-\-url= url ]
.RI [ \-\-branch= branch ]
.RI [ \-\-check\-sync= true | false ]
.RI [ \-\-mirror\-in= true | false ]
.RI [ \-\-merge\-using\-git= true | false ]
.RB [ \-\-enable ]
.RB [ \-\-disable ]
Edit a repo entry in the global store only; project
.I files.json
rows and local sync markers are not updated.
The new name must not match another repo or any collection name.
.B \-\-enable
sets both
.B check_sync_enabled
and
.B mirror_in_enabled
true;
.B \-\-disable
sets both false.
.TP
.BI new " collection"
Also
.BR "n " \-col .
.I name
.RI [ \-\-repos= repo1,repo2 ]
Create a named collection in
.IR collections.json .
Optional
.B \-\-repos=
lists initial members; each must exist in
.IR repos.json .
The name must not match an existing repo or collection.
.TP
.BI remove " collection"
Also
.BR "rm " \-col .
.I name
Remove a collection from
.IR collections.json .
.TP
.BI edit " collection"
Also
.BR "e " \-col .
.I name
.RI [ \-\-rename= new ]
.RI [ \-\-add\-repo= name ]
.RI [ \-\-remove\-repo= name ]
Change a collection; at least one option is required.
.B \-\-add\-repo=
requires the repo in
.IR repos.json .
.B \-\-remove\-repo=
is a no-op if the repo is not listed.
.SS "Self-update"
.TP
.B update
.RI [ \-y " | " \-\-yes ]
Compare the installed version with the latest GitHub release. If a newer release exists and this install can be upgraded automatically (a git checkout of filesync, or a matching
.B .deb
on the release), prompts whether to apply the update:
.B git
pull and
.B make install
from a clone, or
.B dpkg \-i
for the release
.B .deb
(uses
.B sudo
for
.B make install
and
.B dpkg \-i
when
.B sudo
is on
.BR PATH ,
otherwise runs them without elevation). If no update is needed, prints that and exits. If an update is available but cannot be installed automatically from this layout, prints a link to the release page.
.B \-y
and
.B \-\-yes
skip the confirmation prompt and apply immediately when an update is available.
.SH FILES
System metadata directory (default
.BR ~/.filesync\-root ;
see
.BR FILESYNC_HOME ):
.TP
.I system.json
Version and other metadata.
.TP
.I repos.json
Global array of repo definitions (
.BR id ", " check_sync_enabled ", " mirror_in_enabled ", " merge_using_git ", ..." ).
.B merge_using_git
is required on every row; run
.B migrate
to backfill when upgrading.
.TP
.I collections.json
Global array of
.B { "name", "repos" }
objects; used to expand
.B \-\-also=
tokens.
.TP
.I preferences.json
Merged over package defaults;
.I progress_display
.RI ( hidden \| bar \| percent )
for TTY progress on long loops.
.PP
Per project:
.TP
.I .filesync/files.json
Array of file mapping rows (
.BR repo_id
and paths/status fields; the current repo name is not stored here).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B FILESYNC_HOME
Absolute path to the system metadata directory (overrides default
.BR ~/.filesync\-root ).
Intended for tests and automation; avoid per-project shell env if you want the normal shared catalog.
There is no separate pointer file for the system store path.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_REPO_PATH_ANCHOR
Optional absolute directory: used instead of
.B $HOME
when resolving relative
.B path
values in
.IR repos.json
(tests).
.TP
.B FILESYNC_SYSTEM_HOME
Set by the tool to the resolved metadata directory; not an input override.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_PROJECT_ROOT
Project root directory.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_DIR
Path to the
.B .filesync
directory.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_INSTALL_PREFIX
For
.B "filesync update"
from a git checkout when applying an update,
.B PREFIX
passed to
.BR "make install"
when autodetection is wrong.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_VERBOSE
When set to a non-empty value, enables extra informational messages on standard error for commands that support it.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_NO_PROGRESS
When set to
.BR 1 ,
TTY progress is not drawn on standard error (overrides
.IR progress_display ).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
When set to a non-empty value, disables ANSI color in terminal output.
.TP
.B FILESYNC_DEBUG
When set to a non-empty value, commands that use the standard runtime print a short debug line on standard error when a command fails under
.BR "set -e"
(errtrace).
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success, or
.B check
/
.B sync
completed with nothing blocking (or every selected row was skipped because
.B check_sync_enabled
is false for its repo, in which case a hint is printed).
.TP
.B 1
Failure: missing dependencies, invalid or missing configuration, usage errors, or
.B check
/
.B sync
completed with blocking issues or failures. Messages on standard error are prefixed with
.B filesync:
where applicable.
.TP
.B 2
Reserved for auxiliary tooling (e.g. test runner scripts); the
.B filesync
CLI itself uses
.B 1
for invalid options on subcommands such as
.BR update .
.SH SEE ALSO
Extended configuration and environment notes live in
.I docs/configuration.md
in the source repository (the
.B .deb
package ships this manual page, changelog, and copyright; it does not install that Markdown file).
